            "review_id": "REV_14021009_p1_0",
            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_0",
            "review_title": "Review at Blue Whale Restaurant & Bar",
            "review_text": "MJ7788\nHong Kong, China28 contributions\n0\nSeafood dinner with six of us, nice view/location on beach front\nMay 2019 • Friends\nNice seafood, staff are friendly and helpful, even peeled off the tiger prawns for us ^^ Price are reasonable and neatly shows on the menu with photos, and you feel they are honest, even showed us the crab we had chosen and reconfirmed the weight before bringing to the kitchen. \n\n💩Not like the other seafood restaurant also on the other side on the beach called ‘Bien Lon’ 😤😤😤 Very dishonestly bought us different seafood from what we had chosen from the fish tank on the ground floor 👎🏻\n\nAnyway, my friends liked the grilled oysters and fish best (they stuffed some herbs inside the fish, tasted like lemongrass and more) Spring rolls with shrimps were nicely made with cucumber and raw mango strips. Six of us had spent around USD160 with around 10 dishes, some beers and young coconuts \n\nPlease DON’T order the beefsteak, unless you like the dried and chewy texture 😂\n\nToilets are at the basement, better with more light and if it’s dryer on the floor.\nRead more\nWritten May 29, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
